<urn:atm:triage:finding/FNX-024>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FNX-024" ;
  triage:title "PermanentlyFailed attention tombstones have no retirement trigger -- suppression is exempted from pruning but never actually released" ;
  triage:description "Arising from the f642edabe regression review on SOLAR-CDR-009 (arch-ctm deleted the reserved_until<0 sentinel outright rather than replacing it, which fenix caught and solar root-caused with a contract ruling). solar's contract: PermanentlyFailed is terminal for the exact attention item generation only, never for the underlying message/task -- identity is (member, message_id) for the ephemeral lane and (member, task_id, assignment_attempt, assignment_message_id) for the persistent lane. Reassign/Reopen mint a new assignment_attempt and therefore a fresh identity with a fresh budget automatically (verified: reassign_v2 at atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/task_ops.rs:626-644 derives next_attempt via a checked increment). Start/Block/Unblock retain the same attempt and must not reset the budget (verified: task_ops.rs:218,:232 route through plain transition_v2, never touching current_attempt). Because prune_terminal_rows must now exempt PermanentlyFailed rows from generic age/count pruning (required in the current CDR-009 patch, so a load-bearing suppression tombstone cannot be deleted out from under it), those tombstones would otherwise accumulate unboundedly forever -- solar: 'intentionally UNBOUNDED until this finding closes,' not bounded in practice, that characterization must not reach the fix report or docs. AttentionScheduleStore cannot itself decide retirement: ADR-063 D2 gives it only cursors and reservations, explicitly not message or task lifecycle, and its boundary forbids that dependency -- so retirement must be pushed in, not pulled. Required fix shape (solar, adopted by fenix): a push-based, idempotent retirement operation on AttentionScheduleStore. The owning lifecycle/orchestration path (task/message state transitions) supplies the exact typed item identity (AttentionItemIdentity or an equivalent lane-specific typed identity) to this operation AFTER the source transition commits; AttentionScheduleStore deletes or supersedes only its own tombstone for that identity and never queries message or task state, preserving ADR-063 D2. A crash before the retirement call leaves a harmless suppressing tombstone (not a re-armed item); retry/reconciliation simply repeats the idempotent call. Required test coverage: task reassign/reopen retires the old identity's tombstone (new attempt is independently eligible, per FNX already-covered case, but the OLD identity's row must now actually be retired/removed, not merely superseded by a new insert); Start and Unblock must NOT trigger retirement (same attempt, budget must stay suppressed -- overlaps FNX-021's Start marker-clear semantics but is a distinct mechanism, keep implementations apart per fenix's routing note); message retirement is pushed only when the message stops being pending (read or otherwise resolved), not merely on delivery of one reservation attempt. Delivered/Stale row retention remains bounded independently via the existing generic age/count pruning (unaffected -- those two statuses stay ordinarily prunable; only PermanentlyFailed is exempted and needs this push-based retirement instead)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "concurrency-correctness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-storage/src/attention.rs, crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/attention_schedule_store.rs, crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/task_ops.rs, crates/atm-core/src/nudge_dispatch (or equivalent lifecycle/orchestration call site that owns task/message state transitions)" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-10T22:22:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AZ.4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-10T22:11:19Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FNX-024/AZ4-001> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

